         "id": "a",
         "prompt": "Find \\( \\displaystyle\\int_{1}^{-2} f(x)\\,dx \\) and \\( \\displaystyle\\int_{-2}^{3} \\big(2f(x) - 3g(x) + 1\\big)\\,dx \\). Show the work that leads to your answers.",
         "setup_required": false,
         "answer_latex": "\\int_{1}^{-2} f(x)\\,dx = -3, \\quad \\int_{-2}^{3} \\big(2f(x) - 3g(x) + 1\\big)\\,dx = 15",
         "worked_solution": [
            {
               "text": "Adjacent intervals give the integral of f on [-2, 1].",
               "latex": "\\int_{-2}^{1} f(x)\\,dx = 8 - 5 = 3"
            },
            {
               "text": "Reverse the limits.",
               "latex": "\\int_{1}^{-2} f(x)\\,dx = -\\int_{-2}^{1} f(x)\\,dx = -3"
            },
            {
               "text": "Adjacent intervals give the integral of g on [-2, 3].",
               "latex": "\\int_{-2}^{3} g(x)\\,dx = -4 + 6 = 2"
            },
            {
               "text": "Linearity, with the constant 1 integrated over an interval of length 5.",
               "latex": "\\int_{-2}^{3} \\big(2f(x) - 3g(x) + 1\\big)\\,dx = 2(8) - 3(2) + 5 = 15"
            }
         ],
